// Z3 Contract Test: a callee's `ensures` must be assumed at its own call
// site, so the caller can rely on it for a LATER call's `requires`.
// Expected: PASS
//
// `result` used to lower to a symbol literally named "result" -- the same
// name at every call site with an ensures clause, colliding across all of
// them -- and was never substituted to anything, so the fact asserted was
// about a symbol nothing downstream ever referenced. It was also asserted
// only into ctx.z3_solver, which requires/ensures checks never read (each
// builds a fresh Solver; only while-loop invariant proving reads it
// directly). `let y = g(); h(y);` therefore treated `y` as fully free.
package test_composability_ensures_proved

fn g() -> u64 ensures { result == 5 } {
    return 5;
}

fn h(y: u64) requires { y > 0 } { }

pub fn f() {
    let y = g();
    h(y);
}
